**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A kit's experiments and scenes are read and written by typed members over the per-kind verbs (001 §P '`KitProxy` … setups, experiments'; step 127: a kind adds no proxy verb; the S4.3 brief: committing, editing and removing an experiment and saving and loading a scene write and read kit files, and SceneRoundTripTests and ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests are re-pointed at kit files). In `KitContentFiles.fs` (steps 146-147), on one `type KitProxy with` extension, each member documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3: (1) `member this.writeExperiment (experiment : Experiment) : Result<unit, KitError>` renders `experiment.experimentFile.fileText` and writes it with `writeKindFile ExperimentKitFile experiment.id.fileStem` (step 127), replacing a file of that name whole. A `StorageError` of the rendering is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the error's `describe`. (2) `member this.deleteExperiment (id : ExperimentId) : Result<unit, KitError>` is `deleteKindFile ExperimentKitFile id.fileStem`. (3) `member this.readExperiments () : Result<Experiment list, KitError>` reads every stem `listKindFiles ExperimentKitFile` answers, with `readKindFile`, and parses it with `parseExperimentFile`. A refusal, or a file whose experiment's `id.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case, is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and the reason, and the whole read answers it, so the constructor never opens a kit with an experiment left out. The answer is ordered by `id`. (4) `member this.writeScene (name : SceneName) (scene : SceneSnapshot) : Result<unit, KitError>` writes `{ schemaVersion = SceneFile.currentSchemaVersion; name = name; scene = scene }` by `fileText` with `writeKindFile SetupKitFile name.fileStem`, a rendering error mapped as in (1). Two names with one stem (they differ only in characters Windows forbids) share one file, and the later write replaces it. (5) `member this.readScene (name : SceneName) : Result<SceneSnapshot, KitError>` reads `readKindFile SetupKitFile name.fileStem` and answers the parsed file's `scene`; a missing file is `MissingKitFileErr` (step 127) and a refusal is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file. (6) `member this.readSceneNames () : Result<SceneName list, KitError>` parses every setup file and answers the names they hold, in ordinal order; a refused file refuses the read as in (3). Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) every write answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and every read passes, because the members call the proxy's verbs. No cache, retry or other member is added. Tests. `SceneRoundTripTests` and `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` drop their in-memory stores and run over a kit folder: each fact makes `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "<class>", <a new GUID>)` (the `KitProxyFolderTests` precedent, step 126), builds `KitProxy.create` over it and calls `initialiseKit` of a test-local kit file. Each module doc says so in one to three lines. `SceneRoundTripTests` keeps `sceneName` and its fixture elements. `createInMemory round-trips capture-save-load-restore reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings, and view state` becomes `a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state`: `writeScene` of `Experiment A` and the captured scene, then `readSceneNames` answers `[ Experiment A ]`, `readScene` answers the captured scene, the folder holds `Experiment A.setup-json`, and `restoreScene` of it onto `initTableAndElementRotation ()` keeps every assertion. `saveScene overwrites a scene stored under the same name (upsert)` becomes `writing a scene again under its name replaces its kit file`, with the same assertions over `readSceneNames` and `readScene`. `tryLoadScene returns None for a name that was never saved` becomes `reading a scene the kit never held is MissingKitFileErr`. `saveScene rejects a directly-constructed blank name as InvalidScene` is deleted: the store that re-validated a name is gone, and `SceneName.tryCreate` keeps its facts (step 151). It gains `a setup file that does not read refuses the scene list, naming the file`: `Broken.setup-json` written by the test as `{` makes `readSceneNames` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming it. `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` keeps `e1`, `e2` and `e3`; `collectionName`, `snapshotOf` and its `ExperimentCollectionStore` open go. `createInMemory round-trips a collection of E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes, and data attachments` becomes `a kit's experiment files round-trip E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes and data attachments`: `writeExperiment` of E3, E1 and E2, then `readExperiments` answers `[ e1; e2; e3 ]`, and the folder holds `E1.experiment-json`, `E2.experiment-json` and `E3.experiment-json`. `saveCollection overwrites a collection stored under the same name (upsert)` becomes `writing an experiment again replaces its kit file`: E1, then E1 with `CaptureReflected`, reads back as the second. `tryLoadCollection returns None for a name that was never saved` becomes `a kit with no experiment files reads no experiments`: a fresh kit answers `Ok []`. `listCollections enumerates every saved collection and each loads back value-identically` becomes `deleting an experiment removes its kit file and keeps the others`: after E1, E2 and E3, `deleteExperiment (ExperimentId 2)` leaves `readExperiments` answering `[ e1; e3 ]`, and a second delete answers `MissingKitFileErr`. `saveCollection rejects a directly-constructed blank name as InvalidCollection and stores nothing` is deleted, because experiments are named by their ids. It gains `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file`: `E5.experiment-json` written as `{`, and `E6.experiment-json` holding E1's file text, each make `readExperiments` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file; and `a read-only kit refuses experiment and scene writes and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView`, `writeExperiment`, `deleteExperiment` and `writeScene` answer `KitReadOnlyErr`, the folder's files and bytes are unchanged, and `readExperiments` answers what the kit holds.

**Acceptance.** After the typed members land, `KitProxy.writeExperiment`, `deleteExperiment`, `readExperiments`, `writeScene`, `readScene` and `readSceneNames` MUST write, read and delete the kit's experiment and setup files, a file that does not read refusing the whole read, and `SceneRoundTripTests` and `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` MUST run over kit folders; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state`, `writing a scene again under its name replaces its kit file`, `reading a scene the kit never held is MissingKitFileErr`, `a setup file that does not read refuses the scene list, naming the file`, `a kit's experiment files round-trip E1 (full) / E2 (sample-less) / E3 (dark), preserving ordered setups, optional shapes and data attachments`, `writing an experiment again replaces its kit file`, `a kit with no experiment files reads no experiments`, `deleting an experiment removes its kit file and keeps the others`, `an experiment file that does not read, or holds another id, refuses the read, naming the file`, `a read-only kit refuses experiment and scene writes and writes nothing`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.
